# Midnight Tapes - Agent & Coding Assistant Instructions

You are working on "Tiệm Băng Nửa Đêm" (Midnight Tapes), an ambient cathartic web experience.
Always abide by these core directives:

1. GOLDEN RULES ENFORCEMENT:
- Never implement text chat or continuous message exchanges between users.
- Never add user profile pages, personal avatars, or social/Gmail login requirements. Identity is zero-login using anonymous session UUID + backend IP-hash (never store raw IP, never use IP alone as private mailbox key due to shared Wi-Fi/CGNAT).
- Enforce 24-hour time-to-live (TTL) on all recordings and responses.
- Route heavy psychological distress / crisis tapes through the one-shot Psychological First Aid RAG pipeline (grounded coping guidance + hotlines, never an open-ended chatbot).
- Respect the mechanical skeuomorphic feel: every interaction must map to audio feedback and tactile cassette operations.

2. CODE QUALITY & PATTERNS:
- Use TypeScript strictly.
- When writing Web Audio code, ensure proper browser autoplay policy compliance (unlock AudioContext on first user interaction).
- Audio recordings must support up to 7 minutes (420 seconds) for main tapes (with Pause/Resume support) and up to 3 minutes (180 seconds) for voice replies, with precise countdown timers and waveform/VU meter animations.
- Always support cross-platform mobile & desktop (Mobile = Sony Walkman hand-held POV; Desktop = Wooden desk late-night ambient view).

3. TONE OF VOICE:
- All user-facing Vietnamese copy must be warm, serene, poetic, and respectful.
- Avoid robotic or cold clinical jargon.
